TOKEN OPTIMIZATION & REPOSITORY GOVERNANCE
CONTEXT RETRIEVAL & EXPLORATION:

Consult graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md for high-level architecture, module communities, and entry points.

For specific structural queries, execute AST inspection commands (e.g. graphify query "" --terse).

Never perform open-ended file tree dumps (e.g. recursive grep or large find calls).

Inspect files using targeted line slices rather than dumping full file contents.

SURGICAL CODE MODIFICATIONS:

Execute code edits strictly using targeted SEARCH / REPLACE blocks with 3 to 5 lines of surrounding context.

Avoid replacing entire files for localized function or module changes.

COMMAND EXECUTION & LOG HYGIENE:

Avoid dumping large logs; filter noisy build, test, and lint commands using tail or error filters.

Batch sequential shell commands where appropriate.

SECURITY & SECRETS PROTECTION (STRICT):

NEVER inspect, log, commit, or push sensitive credentials (e.g. API keys, passwords, private tokens, internal plans, or environment variables).

Ensure all sensitive configuration files (.env, credentials, secrets) are ignored by git before writing code.

If a task requires an API key, instruct the user to configure it locally via their environment rather than in code.

GIT SAFETY & PERSISTENCE (STRICT):

NEVER execute git commit or git push autonomously.

Only stage (git add) and commit changes when the user explicitly commands it in their prompt.

Keep conversational responses concise: direct answers, 1 to 2 sentence rationale, zero conversational fluff.